# Re-key the stored DEZA walk rows whose key the deployed split no longer builds
# (backend plan 0272). post.sh runs `node deza-keys.js` inside the harvester pod
# after the rollout. For every OFFICIAL_WEB row of the deza-web chain whose
# stored key is entryKey of its stored text, it rebuilds the description, splits
# it with the splitSize of this release, and rewrites the key, the name and the
# size text of each row whose key moved, in one transaction. Nothing is deleted
# or inserted, and no decision, price, availability or presence row changes.
# A key counts as held only by a row that keeps it after every possible move,
# so a chain whose holder moves too is not a collision: the holder moves first,
# in the same run. A moved row whose new key such a row holds, two moved rows
# that give one new key, a swap or a ring of rows that each want the next
# one's key, and every row whose chain ends on one of them, are collisions:
# skipped and counted.
#
# The re-keyed and skipped rows are listed by id and key, never by name, in the
# ConfigMap release-task-0008-record of the namespace (plan 0272, section 4.1).
#
# The deploy unit whose release runs this task (k8s plan 0015 D9).
UNIT="velista"
RUN_UNTIL_STAGING="2026-11-26"
RUN_UNTIL_PRODUCTION="2026-12-03"
# The velista release that carries plans 0266 and 0270 and this task, the
# release task 0007 names too (decision 52a).
PRODUCTION_RELEASE="0.20.0"
# The one database the task writes.
DATABASES="harvester"
#
# The most rows the task may re-key. check.sh counts them with `--count` and
# refuses above this number, and post.sh counts again and passes it to the
# command as `--max`, which refuses too. An empty value is not a number, so
# both scripts refuse it.
#
# Production: the read only recount of 2026-11-19 through the admin API, with
# the selection of this branch, counted 137 moves (125 ACTIVE, 12 UNRESOLVED)
# of 14,350 walk rows: 140 is that, rounded up to the next ten.
#
# Staging: the read only recount of 2026-11-19 counted 137 moves, the same as
# production, so both ceilings are 140. Write another number only after
# reading the count that the check phase prints, never to get past it.
MAX_MOVES_STAGING="140"
MAX_MOVES_PRODUCTION="140"
#
# Walk rows whose key their own text does not build, which the task never
# touches. Production held 0.
MAX_UNKEYED_STAGING="0"
MAX_UNKEYED_PRODUCTION="0"
#
# Collisions, as the top of this file states them, which the task skips
# (decision 50b). Production held 0. One collision also pauses DEZA walks until the
# ceiling is raised: the task then refuses, the moves stay, and the guard
# refuses every DEZA catalog walk. To let a collision through, raise this in a
# commit and link that row by hand.
MAX_COLLISIONS_STAGING="0"
MAX_COLLISIONS_PRODUCTION="0"
